  "steps": [
    "For the sauce, gently cook the shallots, garlic cloves and sesame seeds in the olive oil in a small pot over low heat for 20 to 25 minutes, until soft and golden.",
    "Heat the oven to 400°F.",
    "In a bowl, mix the lamb, parsley, tomato paste, cumin, paprika, salt and pepper. Grate in the onion and garlic and knead gently until combined.",
    "Stuff each pita half with a layer of shredded cheese and a thick layer of the lamb mixture, pressing it in evenly.",
    "Brush the outsides with olive oil and sear in a hot skillet on all sides until browned.",
    "Move the arayes to a baking sheet and bake for 8 to 10 minutes, until the lamb is cooked through and the cheese is melted.",
    "Spread the yogurt on a plate. Squeeze the soft shallots and garlic out of their skins onto the yogurt, add the parsley and a spoonful of the infused oil, and mash it all together.",
    "Serve the arayes hot with the garlic yogurt for dipping."
  ],
  "equipment": [
    "skillet"
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Press the filling right to the edges of the pita so it cooks evenly and holds together.",
    "Keep the sauce oil on low heat so the garlic goes sweet and soft, not browned."
  ],
